---
// Computed at build time, same pattern as the copyright year in Footer.astro.
const birthDate = new Date(2000, 5, 27); // June 27, 2000
const today = new Date();
let age = today.getFullYear() - birthDate.getFullYear();
const hadBirthdayThisYear =
	today.getMonth() > birthDate.getMonth() ||
	(today.getMonth() === birthDate.getMonth() &&
		today.getDate() >= birthDate.getDate());
if (!hadBirthdayThisYear) age--;
---

<section class="section" id="about">
	<div class="section-inner">
		<h2>
			<span class="prompt">&gt;</span>about<span
				class="cursor"
				aria-hidden="true"></span>
		</h2>
		<div class="panel copy" data-reveal>
			<p>
				Software developer is the label I'd reach for first, even though my path
				to it wasn't a straight line: electronics trade school, a couple of
				jobs, then a CS degree. Web is one of several things I dabble in,
				alongside systems and graphics work, so I'm about as comfortable in a
				shader or a memory-mapped register as I am in a Vue component.
			</p>
			<p>
				I'm {age}, Norwegian, and finished a Bachelor's in Programming at NTNU
				(Gjøvik) in 2026. Before that I worked as an IT consultant doing user
				support and network infrastructure. Outside of code: hiking (backpacking
				and wild-camping), militaria collecting, airsoft, and video games.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.copy {
		padding: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2rem);
	}

	.copy p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
</style>
